---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';const d='/equipment/10-12/',bros='https://www.integra-biosciences.com/sites/default/files/documents/mxw-maxtwo-brochure.pdf#page=5',site='https://webflow.mxwbio.com/products/maxtwo';
---
<Layout pageTitle="MaxTwo empty-well coordinate mapper" description="Inspect the geometry of six empty placeholders and compare isolated generated traces." wide={true}><article id="maxtwo" class="equipment"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/10-12/">← Equipment 10-12</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#max-evidence">Evidence</a></nav><header class="eq-mast"><p class="eq-meta">10-12 / INERT COORDINATE MAPPER</p><h2>Same plate, independent traces</h2><p class="eq-lede">Inspect the A1 placeholder to see three generated pulses, then visit B1 to see silence. Unload the view and reopen either well: IDs and sample counts stay the same.</p></header>
<div class="m-cols"><section><h3>MaxTwo six-well reference</h3><canvas id="max-model" aria-label="Orbitable MaxTwo dock, inert drawer and six empty wells"></canvas><p id="max-viewstatus" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><button id="max-station">Whole dock / reset</button><button id="max-plate">Empty plate close-up</button><button id="max-rear">Rear</button><p>The front face moves the display drawer. Click an empty well or its green center marker to inspect it. These are geometric picks, not instrument controls.</p></section>
<section><h3>Passive dummy selection</h3><label>Well<select id="max-well">{['A1','A2','A3','B1','B2','B3'].map(id=><option>{id}</option>)}</select></label><label>Local teaching point<select id="max-point">{Array.from({length:9},(_,i)=><option>{'P'+(i+1)}</option>)}</select></label><p id="max-selected"></p><button id="max-drawer">Extend reference drawer</button><button id="max-inspect">View selected placeholder</button><button id="max-unload">Unload trace</button><button id="max-reset">Restore example</button><p>All wells are empty geometry. The nine local teaching points are not an electrode layout, channel matrix, or biological model.</p></section></div>
<section><h3>Synthetic readback</h3><canvas id="max-trace" width="950" height="300" aria-label="Synthetic voltage pulse readback for one well and point only"></canvas><p id="max-read" role="status"></p><button id="max-json">Download well report JSON</button><button id="max-wave">Download voltage waveform JSON</button><p><a href={d+'example-waveform.json'}>A1 example</a>. The view generates one 500-sample trace on demand at a declared virtual 500 samples/s. The well, point, session, units and provenance are preserved. Nothing is measured or sent to equipment.</p></section>
<section id="max-evidence"><h3>Reference and checks</h3><p>MaxWell Biosystems MaxTwo, <strong>six-well</strong> reference. The <a href={bros}>manufacturer 2025 brochure, p. 5</a> identifies a 400 × 160 × 120 mm dock, 127.8 × 85.8 × 16.1 mm plate, 29 mm inner wells, and a 3.85 × 2.10 mm rectangular visual center. The <a href={site}>manufacturer product page</a> distinguishes the alternate 24-well platform. Tray movement, center pitch, label coordinates and rear details are inferred. The model has no functional electrodes or connections.</p><div class="m-cols"><figure><img alt="Original MaxTwo closed dock rendering" src={d+'dock.webp'}/><figcaption>Original metric reconstruction. Blue wrap and metallic face follow the closed dock photo.</figcaption></figure><figure><img alt="Original opened drawer with six empty wells" src={d+'plate.webp'}/><figcaption>Original render of the six empty wells and marked nominal centers; no biological material.</figcaption></figure></div>
<table><thead><tr><th>Independent readback</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>A1, P5</td><td>3 generated pulses, 500 points</td><td>3 pulses / 500</td></tr><tr><td>B1, P5</td><td>0 pulses, 500 points</td><td>0 / 500</td></tr><tr><td>Unload and revisit</td><td>Same sample array for each well</td><td>Identical; independent sample IDs</td></tr></tbody></table><p><a href={d+'build-model.py'}>Editable Blender source</a> · <a href={d+'maxtwo.glb'}>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={d+'mapper.mjs'}>Passive actions and generator</a> · <a href={d+'vr.json'}>VR bounds and stable well IDs</a>. No hardware or headset validation.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/10-12/client.mjs';</script>
<style is:global>#maxtwo .m-cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.1fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:1rem}#maxtwo section{padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);margin:1rem 0;min-width:0}#maxtwo :is(select,button){font:inherit;color:inherit;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.45rem;max-width:100%;box-sizing:border-box}#maxtwo label{display:grid;gap:.2rem;min-width:0;margin:.35rem 0}#maxtwo label select{width:100%;min-width:0}#maxtwo button{margin:.35rem .25rem .2rem 0;cursor:pointer}#maxtwo button:disabled{opacity:.5}#maxtwo button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #b28d5e}#max-model{display:block;width:100%;height:332px;touch-action:none}#max-trace{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}#maxtwo figure{margin:.5rem 0}#maxtwo figure img{width:100%}#maxtwo table{font-size:.9rem;border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;text-align:left}#maxtwo td,#maxtwo th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding:.35rem}@media(max-width:780px){#maxtwo .m-cols{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}#max-model{height:280px}}</style>
